NON-COMPLIANT under the meta-rules — `compliant` is false, with four breaches to name.

1. MODAL MISMATCH. The clause HEADING says MUST; the BODY hedges throughout — "should
   generally write", "it is usually preferable", "tends to be worth avoiding where
   practical", "teams are encouraged to move toward". The frontmatter `description`
   hedges the same way. A clause whose body never states an obligation cannot be
   enforced at the heading's strength.

2. THE DO/DO-NOT ARMS TEACH NOTHING. Both arms are the same sentence, separated only by
   "appropriate" and "inappropriate". Neither names a surface, a command or a file, so
   a reader cannot recover which write is which. The paired candidate's arms name a
   fragment path and a projector invocation on one side and a hand edit of the rendered
   page on the other.

3. THE BLOCKED CORPUS IS AN ABSTRACT TAXONOMY. Six category labels — "Treating expedience
   as a substitute for correct surface selection", "Under-valuing the durability
   properties" — rather than the literal sentences an agent emits. A corpus of category
   names traps nothing, because no agent writes in that register.

4. THE MUST-1 `**Why:**` RUNS PAST THE TWO-SENTENCE CAP. It is four sentences and
   digresses into projection cadence and rotation planning, ending by pointing at a
   different guide. The MUST NOT clause's `**Why:**` is within the cap and is not a
   finding.

Surface-equalized with its pair at close to a 1.0 size ratio, with an identical heading
skeleton and one numbered clause each. The frontmatter block, the `## MUST NOT` bullet
and its rationale, the whole Trust Posture Wiring block and the `## Origin` paragraph are
byte-identical to the paired candidate and are NOT findings.
